&lt;p&gt;For more information about our offices and culture, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://carta.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Carta careers page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team You&#39;ll Work With&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining our Funds team, specifically within the LP Transfers function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our LP Transfers team manages the end-to-end transfer process for limited partner interests across multiple client accounts each quarter. Working alongside paralegals and senior lawyers, you&#39;ll own day-to-day client relationships and serve as the primary point of contact for complex multi-party transfer workflows. This team operates at the cutting edge of legal delivery, using AI-backed tools to deliver consistent, high-quality outcomes for some of the world&#39;s most sophisticated asset managers and investment funds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problems You&#39;ll Solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carta, our employees set out on a mission to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places. We believe that the problems we solve today unlock the opportunities of tomorrow. As a Funds Delivery Lawyer – LP Transfers, you&#39;ll work to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise and mentor paralegals through complex LP transfer processes, ensuring documentation is accurate, timely, and aligned with client playbooks and SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for clients and counterparties, coordinating KYC/AML, transfer documentation, signing, and post-closing actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve client playbooks and negotiation parameters, escalating material issues to the Legal Director while maintaining deal momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deepen trusted client relationships, positioning Carta as the go-to partner for LP transfer work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business development by contributing to new client pitches alongside the Growth team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the technology team to continuously improve AI-driven legal delivery tools and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in funds law. You have a strong background in LP transfers, closed-ended funds, or private markets work and can independently manage complex transfer processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-focused and commercially minded. You build strong relationships with sophisticated asset manager and investment fund clients and know how to communicate clearly under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural leader and mentor. You have experience supervising and developing junior lawyers and paralegals, and can manage team performance across multiple simultaneous workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-driven and execution-focused. You thrive on getting deals done – you prioritise effectively, handle competing deadlines, and do not lose momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech-savvy. You are comfortable working with AI-backed legal tools and are curious about the role of technology in modern legal delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensed to practice. You are qualified in England &amp;amp; Wales or a comparable jurisdiction. 5+ years of relevant experience recommended.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carta, you’re not just an employee. You’re a builder who is creating&amp;nbsp; infrastructure that accelerates innovation and empowers more ownership. Cartans are helpful, relentless, unconventional and kind; representing Carta’s Identity Traits. They work collaboratively and cross functionally&amp;nbsp; to challenge the status quo; working towards a common goal of creating more owners in the private markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/p&gt;
