&lt;p&gt;At Carta, our employees set out on a mission to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places. We believe that the problems we solve today unlock the opportunities of tomorrow. As a Lead Product Marketing Manager focused on our Carta Law segment, you&#39;ll work to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Compliance &amp;amp; Market Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply a deep focus on governance, risk, and compliance (GRC) to product positioning, while serving as a key product subject matter expert at company and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Launch Strategy &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner across GTM and R&amp;amp;D teams to tier launches, establish Bills of Materials (BOMs), and manage execution from initial brief through post-launch analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Asset Creation &amp;amp; Creative Briefing:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop high-performing product collateral, multimedia, and sales enablement assets in close collaboration with Creative, and Brand Strategy teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Alignment &amp;amp; Campaign Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate product roadmaps with demand generation, integrated marketing, and paid channels to drive campaign success, lifecycle marketing, and event presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; Messaging Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and evolve the core product narrative, value proposition, and market positioning for Carta Law, translating complex legal/regulatory features into clear value for buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Voice of Customer &amp;amp; Win/Loss Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct ongoing customer interviews, and win/loss studies to uncover buyer friction and feed insights directly into the R&amp;amp;D team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
