&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining our Carta Law team, specifically within the Contracts - North Americas function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Contracts team manages the full lifecycle of commercial contracts for clients – from first review through to execution. You&#39;ll be the direct day-to-day contact for sophisticated investment fund and asset manager clients, working alongside fellow lawyers and paralegals. This team delivers high volumes of pre-M&amp;amp;A contract work at speed, supported by AI-backed tools including Carta&#39;s proprietary platform, Ava.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problems You&#39;ll Solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carta, our employees set out on a mission to unlock the power of equity ownership for more people in more places. We believe that the problems we solve today unlock the opportunities of tomorrow. As a Contract Solutions Counsel on the Contracts team, you&#39;ll work to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage high volumes of pre-M&amp;amp;A contracts – including NDAs, confidentiality agreements, NRLs, joinders, and engagement letters – directly liaising with counterparties and adhering to agreed turnaround times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary day-to-day contact for clients, building trusted advisor relationships with sophisticated investment funds and asset managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update client playbooks on an ongoing basis, ensuring consistency and quality across all contract negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with and mentor junior lawyers and paralegals, reviewing their work and contributing to a high-performing team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the continuous improvement of Carta&#39;s legal technology suite, identifying ways to innovate using AI-backed tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercially minded and client-focused. &lt;/strong&gt;You communicate legal advice crisply and concisely, building strong relationships with sophisticated financial services clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced in transactional law. &lt;/strong&gt;You have 4+ years of post law school corporate or transactional experience, with a track record of independently negotiating pre-M&amp;amp;A contracts (NDAs, NRLs, joinders, engagement letters).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiar with financial services. &lt;/strong&gt;You have experience working with asset managers, investment banks, or other financial services firms and understand their expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Law Degree and licensed to practice. &lt;/strong&gt;You are licensed to practice law in the Americas (US/Canada).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech-savvy and adaptable. &lt;/strong&gt;You are comfortable working with and evolving a legal technology suite (e.g. AI tools, HighQ), and an interest in legal tech or AI is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A self-starter who owns their work. &lt;/strong&gt;You thrive in a fast-paced environment, prioritize effectively, and are always looking for ways to improve and innovate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
